From 2f0acf4dc463c972b38a82c362d4a187276c3013 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: knfsd-fuzz <knfsd-fuzz@localhost>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 20:59:51 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] sunrpc: attribute NFSv4.1 server callbacks to the program
 that caused them

A callback runs long after the request that caused it has replied, in a
workqueue worker and in rpciod, so none of it was covered by the request's
remote section.  A missing PC could not be read as "not executed".

Record the program behind a callback when it is queued, from the section the
caller is running, and open a short remote section for each step of it.

The record holds a generation reference and no outstanding Token.  A pending
callback therefore never delays FINISH.  Each section mints its own Token and
Ticket from that reference and is refused once the generation is closing,
committed or aborted; the late work is counted, not attributed to whichever
generation is open at that moment.  The first owner of a callback wins when
events merge into one.

kcov: kcov_request_token_generation_get() and
kcov_request_try_get_section_token() create the reference and the Token; the
section helpers look at the section the current task runs, so a nested call
for the same owner joins it instead of starting a second Ticket.

sunrpc: the owner is carried on the rpc_task.  __rpc_execute() opens a section
around each FSM step, and the resource release and the calldata release open
one too.  receive_cb_reply() collects the reply for the owner of the matching
request; it leaves queue_lock with the request pinned to start the section and
checks the request again afterwards.  rpc_free_task() reads the owner before
the release op because the task can be embedded in its calldata.

nfsd: nfsd4_run_cb() stores the owner, nfsd4_run_cb_work() runs inside a
section, and nfsd41_destroy_cb() detaches the owner before RUNNING is cleared.

Also add kcov_request_handle_id() so lane_owner_work() builds without
CONFIG_KCOV.  Selftests cover the Token and Ticket life cycle.
